{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The powered USB hub fits my purchases of a USB expansion card and USB network adapters because it could help me connect those accessories, although ten ports may exceed my needs.",
    "The wired earbuds and mouse fit my history of buying practical computer accessories, but that relevance alone would not make me buy them without a replacement need."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Streaming sticks and a smart speaker do not solve the computer connection needs reflected in my purchases, and I have no current reason to add them.",
    "A small-tablet mount does not imply a large-TV mounting project, and owning a DVI cable does not establish that I need HDMI. The device and connection have to match.",
    "The memory card could be useful for some devices, but my history does not establish a current need for that storage format."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in specific computer accessories seems to have been stretched into an interest in electronics generally.",
    "Connections such as cable to cable or mount to mount seem to matter too much when the products serve different devices and purposes."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several of my purchases help add ports or network connections to computers, which makes a useful connection accessory more relevant than home entertainment equipment.",
    "I buy infrequently and need a concrete reason to act; a related accessory is not automatically something I need to replace or upgrade.",
    "Compatibility matters: my history names particular ports, devices, and operating systems, so a broadly similar product may still be unsuitable."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my practical computer accessory needs but extended them too broadly into unrelated electronics and purchases without a current purpose."
}"}
